# Copy this file to ".env" only if you need it. For this project, the two
# integrations are configured in content, not env vars:
#
#   Lemon Squeezy checkout link  → PUBLIC_LEMONSQUEEZY_CHECKOUT_URL below
#   Kit (ConvertKit) form action → src/content/brand/site.json  (newsletter.kitAction)
#
# Both are PUBLIC values (safe to commit) — no secrets live in this repo.

# Amplitude Browser SDK — analytics.
# This is Amplitude's *browser* API key: it is public by design and safe to
# expose in client-side JS and to commit here. It is NOT a secret key.
# Analytics only initialise in a production build AND when this is set, so
# localhost stays untracked. For the live site, set the same variable in the
# Cloudflare Pages project → Settings → Environment variables.
PUBLIC_AMPLITUDE_API_KEY=

# Lemon Squeezy checkout link for the buy buttons (hero + Featured Adventure).
# Paste the public "Buy now" URL from your Lemon Squeezy product, e.g.
#   https://kitchentablewonders.lemonsqueezy.com/buy/xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx
# This is a PUBLIC link (it is in the page HTML) — not a secret.
# Leave it as "#" until the store is live: the buttons stay clickable and go
# nowhere harmful instead of 404ing, and the Lemon Squeezy overlay stays off.
# Set the same variable in Cloudflare Pages → Settings → Environment variables.
PUBLIC_LEMONSQUEEZY_CHECKOUT_URL=#

